========================================================================
what v4 stage two found, in plain English
========================================================================

lstm (lstm, 327k):
  Right after a flip the sign is readable from h at 50%; by 200+ frames later it is 71%. One frame of z gives 59% and shuffled labels give 56%.
  Of that, 52% is memory of the contact itself and 73% is what a cold-started pass can infer from the motion alone.
  There is no memory to decay: even immediately after the flip the sign is not readable above the shuffled-label null.
  Intervening on the contact flips the dreamed curvature on 47% of pairs (chance 50%).

transformer (transformer, 571k):
  Right after a flip the sign is readable from h at 50%; by 200+ frames later it is 55%. One frame of z gives 59% and shuffled labels give 55%.
  Of that, 52% is memory of the contact itself and 70% is what a cold-started pass can infer from the motion alone.
  There is no memory to decay: even immediately after the flip the sign is not readable above the shuffled-label null.
  Intervening on the contact flips the dreamed curvature on 41% of pairs (chance 50%).

